The university library provides a Study Room Booking Service to enrolled students. Students may request a room through the library desk or through an online form. To make a reservation, they must provide their student identifier, the preferred date and time, the expected duration, and the number of participants.

Library staff verify whether the student is eligible to use study rooms and whether an appropriate room is available. Some rooms are reserved for group work and may only be booked by at least three students. If the request can be accepted, the student receives confirmation including the room number and access instructions. If the requested room or time slot is unavailable, library staff may suggest an alternative.

On the day of the reservation, students check in at the library desk. If they do not arrive within 15 minutes of the reserved time, the room becomes available to other students. At the end of the booking period, the room must be left in appropriate condition; library staff may record any issues or damages.
